# Expectation record for 09_optimization_levels/001_arithmetic_invariance.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 001_arithmetic_invariance
area               = 09_optimization_levels
description        = Integer arithmetic results identical at -O0, -O1 and -O2, folded and volatile-runtime variants
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Free of undefined and unspecified behaviour. No signed overflow: 1000+337, 2000-663 and
191*7 are far inside int range, and 1234567891011LL+9876543210LL is far inside long long
range. Negation operand is 1337, not INT_MIN. Shift counts are 3 and 2 on 32-bit unsigned
operands, so strictly in range and with no signed-shift question. Division and modulo use
divisor 7, so no division by zero and no INT_MIN/-1 case. No pointer arithmetic, no
aliasing violation, no read of uninitialized storage, no object modified twice between
sequence points, and no dependence on padding bytes or on relative addresses.
Several volatile objects are read within a single expression; their relative order is
unspecified, but no volatile object is modified anywhere in the program, so every read of
a given object yields the same value and the printed output does not depend on the
ordering.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
No implementation-defined behaviour is observed. Widths are normalized: only int, unsigned
int and long long are used, and long is never used because sizeof(long) is 4 on i686 and 8
on the other three targets. Plain char is not used, so the measured plain-char signedness
difference (signed on x86-64 and i686, unsigned on AArch64 and RISC-V 64) cannot be
observed. No address, pointer value, sizeof or _Alignof result is printed. No floating
point is used. Unsigned results are printed with %u and long long with %lld, both of fixed
width on all four targets.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
add folded=1337 runtime=1337 equal=1
sub folded=1337 runtime=1337 equal=1
mul folded=1337 runtime=1337 equal=1
div folded=1337 runtime=1337 equal=1
mod folded=3 runtime=3 equal=1
neg folded=-1337 runtime=-1337 equal=1
shl folded=1336 runtime=1336 equal=1
shr folded=1337 runtime=1337 equal=1
and folded=15728880 runtime=15728880 equal=1
or  folded=4293984240 runtime=4293984240 equal=1
xor folded=4278255360 runtime=4278255360 equal=1
not folded=4294901760 runtime=4294901760 equal=1
wide folded=1244444434221 runtime=1244444434221 equal=1
END
